# Tooltip text — 14px

Every hover tooltip's message text (the dark bubble shown on hover of an info
icon, truncated link/cell, disabled action, chart bar, etc.) uses **14px**
text, never 12px/13px.

- Shared component: `src/components/HLTooltip.jsx` — its bubble is
  `text-[14px]`. Prefer this component (directly, or via `SectionInfoTip`)
  for any new tooltip instead of hand-rolling a `bg-gray-900` popup.
- If a tooltip must be hand-rolled (e.g. a `group-hover:opacity-100` bubble
  tied to a chart bar or table cell), it still must use `text-[14px]` for the
  message text.

## Not covered by this rule

- Rich info popovers with their own internal type scale (e.g. a metrics
  breakdown card shown on hover, with a label + big number + description) —
  those follow their own component's typography, not a single tooltip-text size.
- The small icon glyph inside a custom `InfoTooltip`'s "i" circle (that's an
  icon, not tooltip body text).

## Before finishing tooltip work

- [ ] Any new/edited tooltip bubble text is `text-[14px]`, not 12/13px.
- [ ] Prefer `HLTooltip` / `SectionInfoTip` over a hand-rolled popup.
